    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vastātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				laying waste</i>, <i>desolating</i>, <i>ravaging</i>, <i>devastation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 2, 8, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. Or. ad Caes. 1, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">villarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 7,
					15</span></i>
			 11; 10, 4, 7; <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 4, 14</span></i>: Italiam a
			vastatione defendere, Planc. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 15, 4</span></i>.—<i>Plur</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intactum vastationibus regnum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
